From fd52a2266de2f0936333964e2a064c66f351903a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:07:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: Options > Graphics no longer crashes, one open per
 file, a log per start, a texture-free depth pass

- Options > Graphics crashed (t27-t28): the Options screen takes options.bmp out of front-end
  set 11; the GRAPHICS screen loads set 11 again, which is still loaded, so nothing reloads the
  taken file, FrontLoader_TakeFile returns 0 and DownloadBMP16x2 read through it. A missing image
  is now logged and skipped (the background on screen stays).
- Game files: one sceIoOpen a load (t28 looked the file up three times: size, first bytes, read;
  ~200 ms each for the files in Data/): size by sceIoLseek, first bytes and data by sceIoPread
  on that handle, closed by the read.
- Logs: each start writes ux0:data/THPS/logs/thps_YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS.log (the newest 10 kept)
  instead of appending to thps.log; the writer syncs at most once a second (and at exit).
- Batched 3D: the depth pass of the opaque faces without transparent texels uses the draw
  vertex shader with a fragment shader that reads no texture (the colour writes are masked off
  there), compiled last (THPS_GL_DEPTHFS=0: the no-discard program as before).
- THPS_GL_GPUTIME=1 (a measurement): glFinish before the swap, "[gpu]" every 60 frames.
